%% Demand Forecast sequence through SPPG routes and Forecast service
sequenceDiagram
    actor SPPG as SPPG User
    actor KDKMP as KDKMP User
    participant UI as React/Inertia UI
    participant Route as routes/web.php + auth/role middleware
    participant C as DemandForecastController
    participant KC as KDKMP ForecastController
    participant Action as DemandForecastActionController
    participant Policy as DemandForecastPolicy
    participant S as DemandForecastService
    participant Readiness as Readiness records / invalidation logic
    participant Support as Audit / Notification / Derived Observation
    participant DB as PostgreSQL

    SPPG->>UI: Enter Forecast payload
    UI->>Route: POST /sppg/forecasts
    Route->>C: store()
    C->>Policy: authorize create for SPPG organization
    C->>S: createDraft command
    S->>DB: transaction + validate canonical commodity/unit/time
    S->>DB: INSERT demand_forecasts (DRAFT, version 1)
    S->>Support: audit
    S-->>UI: DRAFT Forecast

    SPPG->>UI: Publish Forecast
    UI->>Route: POST /sppg/forecasts/{forecast}/publish
    Route->>Action: publish()
    Action->>Policy: authorize owner SPPG
    Action->>S: publish command
    S->>DB: lock Forecast
    S->>DB: verify active PRIMARY supply-network relationship
    S->>DB: UPDATE status=PUBLISHED, published_at, version++
    S->>Support: audit + derived observation after commit
    S-->>UI: published Forecast

    KDKMP->>UI: View published Forecast
    UI->>Route: GET /kdkmp/forecasts/{forecast}
    Route->>KC: show()
    KC->>Policy: authorize read-only KDKMP visibility
    KC->>DB: read Forecast and allowed aggregate context
    KC-->>UI: read-only Inertia page

    SPPG->>UI: Revise published Forecast
    UI->>Route: POST /sppg/forecasts/{forecast}/revise
    Route->>Action: revise()
    Action->>Policy: authorize owner SPPG
    Action->>S: revisePublished command
    S->>DB: lock Forecast + optimistic version validation
    S->>DB: UPDATE payload + version++
    S->>Readiness: invalidate/mark stale previous approved readiness when required
    Readiness->>DB: persist legitimate readiness invalidation/revision effects
    S->>Support: audit + notifications + new derived observation
    S-->>UI: revised PUBLISHED Forecast

    alt Close
        SPPG->>Route: POST /sppg/forecasts/{forecast}/close
        Route->>Action: close()
        Action->>S: close command
        S->>DB: UPDATE PUBLISHED -> CLOSED
    else Cancel
        SPPG->>Route: POST /sppg/forecasts/{forecast}/cancel
        Route->>Action: cancel()
        Action->>S: cancel command
        S->>DB: reject if accepted fallback allocation prevents cancellation
        S->>DB: otherwise UPDATE DRAFT/PUBLISHED -> CANCELLED
    end
